{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgucHNnF1J1xYXoZEujyN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the route to `route.camel.yaml`. I haven't run it or checked it against a Camel 4.22 runtime.\n\nIt reads from `direct:pick-list` and sends each message to the `sftp` endpoint with these settings:\n\n| Requirement | Option used |\n|---|---|\n| Host, port and directory | `sftp:warehouse.trailhead.example:22//inbound/picklists`. The double slash makes `/inbound/picklists` an absolute path; a single slash would make it relative to the user's home directory. |\n| User | `username: trailhead` |\n| Password | `password: \"{{warehouse.password}}\"`, filled in from the `warehouse.password` property |\n| Temporary name while uploading | `tempPrefix: \".uploading-\"`. Camel writes `.uploading-<name>` and renames it to `<name>` once the upload finishes. |\n| Fail if the file already exists | `fileExist: Fail`. With a temporary name in use, Camel checks whether the final file name exists before it uploads. |\n| Strict host key checking | `strictHostKeyChecking: \"yes\"`. The value is quoted so YAML reads it as text, not as true/false. |\n\n**Before you deploy:** with strict host key checking on, the connection is refused unless the warehouse's host key is already trusted. By default Camel looks for it in `~/.ssh/known_hosts` for the user running the route. To use a different source, add the `knownHostsFile` or `knownHostsUri` option.\n\nMessages need a file name to land under. Set the `CamelFileName` header before the upload, or Camel will name the file after the message ID."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1201,"cache_read_input_tokens":4589,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1201},"output_tokens":534,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standar